 the lone 0.6 mm/0.3 mm-drill via at (113,100), and the saved B.Cu zone fill with thermal spokes at J1.3; no redundant track exists. Connectivity holds as saved (DRC 0 unconnected items), but the single-point dependency and reliance on a fill state the toolchain is forbidden to regenerate is an established, evidence-backed robustness concern. Canonical for this issue.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"segment uuid 7deb1fb0 (110.95,100)-(113,100) net GND; via uuid b71a70d7 (at 113 100) (drill 0.3); zone uuid 38a83012 filled_polygon spoke vertices around (99.870591,104.597037)-(100.129408,105.562962) at J1 pad 3\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"tracks[] via entry at [113.0,100.0]; zones[0] filled:true net GND layers B.Cu\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"unconnected_items: []\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"circuit/gnd-single-path-zone-fill\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"duplicate_of\":\"physical/PHY-01\",\"reason\":\"Same defect as physical/PHY-01: identical via (b71a70d7 at 113,100), identical zone (38a83012), identical condition (GND return to J1.3 depends solely on one via plus the saved zone fill) and identical mechanism (refill or via compromise opens the GND net). PHY-01 is retained as canonical because it carries the higher (minor) severity and the more complete copper-path evidence.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"via (at 113 100) (drill 0.3) net GND; zone 38a83012 filled_polygon thermal-spoke coordinates around (xy 99.870591 104.597037)...(xy 100.129408 105.562962)\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"tracks[] via entry at [113.0,100.0]; zones[0] filled:true, net GND\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/PHY-02\",\"disposition\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"Verified in the native board file: vertical /OUT segment a6dab0b4 ends at (107.5,100), which is not a pad or shared endpoint but lies strictly inside segment 69a2edc1 (105.9125,100)-(109.05,100) on the same net, layer, and y-coordinate with full 0.25 mm width overlap. Electrically sound as saved (DRC 0 unconnected items), but the connectivity is positional rather than topological, a real maintenance hazard. Supported singleton finding preserved at info severity.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"segment uuid a6dab0b4 (107.5,102.54)-(107.5,100) net /OUT landing mid-body on segment uuid 69a2edc1 (105.9125,100)-(109.05,100) net /OUT\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"unconnected_items: []\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/PHY-03\",\"disposition\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"Verified: work/geometry/console.log contains three non-fatal 'PROPERTY_ENUM(): No enum choices defined' assertion failures from pcbnew internals, and execution.json records a non-empty stderr hash despite exit code 0 and a pass verdict. The probe's output was independently corroborated against the raw board file (exactly five segments, all width 0.25 mm; pads, via, and zone match), so the geometry pass stands for this run, but the tool-health concern is established and must be recorded for future runs where hand-verification is infeasible. Canonical for this issue.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/geometry/console.log\",\"locator\":\"lines 2-4: assert \\\"m_choices.GetCount() > 0\\\" failed in PROPERTY_ENUM()\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/execution.json\",\"locator\":\"stderr_sha256 ecfdabc9a488fbdbeb42728b58080ecf903a12f0cabcb48d0622d8aa9f2d1a1e (non-empty), exit_code 0\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"five (segment ... (width 0.25)) entries (uuids ae12bf6f, 69a2edc1, 8b528360, a6dab0b4, 7deb1fb0), one via, one zone — matches geometry.json\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"circuit/geometry-probe-assert-noise\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"duplicate_of\":\"physical/PHY-03\",\"reason\":\"Same observation as physical/PHY-03: the identical three PROPERTY_ENUM assertion messages in work/g